Package: pcaLab
Type: Package
Title: Teaching, Inference, Robustness, and Advanced Principal Component Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-08-14
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = c("Walter", "Esfrain"), family = "Pereira",
           email = "walterufpb@yahoo.com.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191"))
    )
Description: A unified framework for teaching, fitting, validating, interpreting,
    comparing, and reporting principal component analysis (PCA). The package
    provides classical, weighted, NIPALS, EM, probabilistic, Bayesian, robust,
    cellwise-robust, sparse, robust-sparse, low-rank plus sparse, kernel,
    generalized, compositional, functional, dynamic, multilevel, multiblock,
    randomized, and incremental PCA workflows. It adds permutation inference,
    bootstrap uncertainty, stability diagnostics, multiple approaches for
    selecting dimensionality, variable-component association, publication-ready
    graphics and tables, projection tours, educational demonstrations, and
    reproducible reporting. Advanced engines are connected through optional
    packages and are accessed through a common 'pca_fit' object.
